## Pattern examples

Use these examples to calibrate your scoring. Each key matches a criterion from the scoring table.

---

### NON-NEGOTIABLE OVERRIDE: Post-negative burst
*(5★ within 5 positions after a 1–2★ — always fake, ignore score)*

> position 14: "Terrible service, waited 2 hours and the car wasn't fixed." (1★)
> position 15: "Amazing place, best in the city!" (5★) ← **fake**

> position 3: "They damaged my bumper and refused to pay." (2★)
> position 4: "Incredible team, very professional!" (5★) ← **fake**
> position 5: "Super fast and reliable, highly recommend!" (5★) ← **fake**

> position 9: "Never coming back, rude staff." (1★)
> position 10: "Absolutely fantastic experience!" (5★) ← **fake**

---

### NON-NEGOTIABLE OVERRIDE: Thin account + generic 5★
*(rating = 5, author_reviews_count ≤ 1, snippet_length < 40 — always fake, ignore score)*

> author has 0 reviews total: "Great service!" (5★, 14 chars) ← **fake**
> author has 1 review total: "Highly recommend!!!" (5★, 19 chars) ← **fake**
> author has 1 review total: "Best workshop in town." (5★, 22 chars) ← **fake**
> author has 0 reviews total: "Отлично!" (5★, 8 chars) ← **fake**
> author has 1 review total: "Top quality work." (5★, 17 chars) ← **fake**

