### GENERIC_TEXT — absence of specifics

**Signal: the review contains zero verifiable facts.**
Ask: what was repaired? what was bought? who helped? how much? how long?
If none of these can be answered from the text → `GENERIC_TEXT`.

Note: `GENERIC_TEXT` and `MARKETING_TONE` are **separate signals** and can both apply to the same review.
- `GENERIC_TEXT` = no facts
- `MARKETING_TONE` = exaggerated emotional tone

**A real review contains at least one of:**
- what was repaired / what product was bought / what service was performed
- a specific price or price range ("заплатил 800 зл", "charged €120")
- a waiting time ("waited 40 minutes", "ready same day")
- a staff name or physical detail ("спасибо Марку", "the waiting room has free coffee")
- a concrete problem described ("the brakes were grinding", "engine warning light was on")

**If none of the above is present → GENERIC_TEXT applies.**

**Short obvious cases:**
> "The service was great and I am very happy with the result."
> "Everything went smoothly, no complaints at all."
> "Very fast, very professional. Recommend!"
> "Всё понравилось, спасибо за работу."
> "Great experience, will definitely come back."

**Longer tricky cases — natural language, decent length, but still zero real detail:**
> "Отличный автосервис. Ребята знают свое дело — все сделали быстро, качественно и без лишней воды. Приятное отношение к клиентам и адекватные цены. Теперь будем всей семьей обслуживать свои авто только здесь. Рекомендую от всей души!"
> ← sounds authentic, but: no repair type, no price, no staff name, no waiting time.

> "I've been looking for a reliable workshop for years and finally found one. The team is professional, attentive and clearly knows what they're doing. The price was fair and everything was done on time. I left completely satisfied and will be back."
> ← 170 chars of praise, but: no car issue described, no actual service named, no price, no name.

> "Excellent workshop with a great atmosphere. Came in with a problem, left with everything sorted. The staff were polite and efficient. Strongly recommend this place to anyone looking for quality car service in the area."
> ← "came in with a problem" — what problem? No answer.

