### LONG_TEXT — review over 450 characters (real signal)

> "I brought my car in for brake work on a Tuesday morning. The mechanic, Marek, explained clearly what needed replacing and showed me the worn pads. The job took about two hours and the price matched the estimate — 680 PLN all in. No surprises. The waiting area is clean and there's decent coffee. I'll be back for the next service."

> "We visited with a reservation for a birthday dinner. The starter — beetroot soup — was excellent but the main course arrived lukewarm. The waiter apologized and offered a discount without us asking. That kind of honesty keeps us coming back despite the small hiccup. The wine list is short but reasonably priced. Parking is easy on weekdays."

> "I've been using this pharmacy for about two years now. The pharmacist always takes time to explain drug interactions, which I really appreciate given that I take three different prescriptions. Twice I've had them flag a potential issue that my doctor missed. The prices are mid-range and waiting times are usually under 10 minutes."

> "Brought the car in after the engine warning light came on. They ran a diagnostic (350 PLN), found a faulty oxygen sensor, ordered the part and had it fitted by Friday — total cost 820 PLN. Communication throughout was clear — they called twice with updates. Only minor issue: the car came back slightly dusty inside. Nothing major."

> "I ordered a custom sofa from this workshop. The initial consultation took an hour — they showed fabric samples, discussed dimensions and delivery timing. The sofa arrived 3 weeks later as promised. The stitching is clean and the foam density is exactly what I asked for. One leg was slightly uneven but they sent someone to fix it within 2 days. Very satisfied overall."

